  message: "DONE — PR merged to dev (a95d6d87c6, fix(coherence)). Executed audit-0013's ratified Cluster 27D fold across all three IDL analyzers whose positional-helper emit sites the grep diagnostics missed:\n  - proto.py: service -> kind='interface', rpc -> kind='method' (a service member), each + meta['framework_role'].\n  - thrift.py: service -> kind='interface' + meta['framework_role']='service' (emit site was a NESTED closure make_symbol, invisible even to the WI-zipis within-module engine — fixed directly here; noted as a nested-helper engine gap for the gate PR).\n  - smithy.py: service -> kind='interface' + meta['framework_role']='service' (merged into the existing traits meta).\nMechanism: each emit helper (_make_proto_symbol / make_symbol / _extract_shape) gained a framework_role param threading the role into Symbol.meta.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (this item changes runtime Symbol.kind, so behavioral not proxy): the WI-zipis Symbol.kind helper-descent census drops 8->5 — proto rpc/service, thrift service, smithy service all GONE. Folded-contract tests assert kind=='interface'/'method' + meta['framework_role'] and pass; full affected suite 3670 passed / 0 failed; proto/thrift/smithy source 100% coverage. Edge.evidence_type helper axis stays clean (0).\n\naudit-0013 CORRECTED: the stale 'zero-producer / RESOLVED' verdict for rpc/service (doc-RESOLVED but producer-UNRESOLVED) is dated-corrected; rpc fold_target function->method (service member); the literal-grep is noted INSUFFICIENT for the positional-helper form (the WI-zipis descend sweep is authoritative). check-audit-findings green.\n\nRESIDUAL (NOT this item — next drain unit): the census's remaining 5 are OUT of audit-0013 scope — smithy structure/list/map (IDL type-shape kinds) + powershell filter/workflow (function-like) — each needs a register-vs-fold verdict, not a ratified fold."  # ac4f
